<header class="site-header">
  {%- comment -%}
    The wordmark unfolds letter by letter on load — ericman.com's origami
    effect, ported in slice 3h. Built from site.title rather than hardcoded, so
    renaming the site renames the animation with it.

    Two things Cobalt's Liquid does here that are worth knowing, both found by
    probing rather than assumed:

      * Splitting on an empty string yields a LEADING and a TRAILING empty
        entry. "Eric Man" comes back as 10 entries, not 8. Rendering those
        would put two empty spans inside the link and, worse, push every
        letter's delay one step late — so they are skipped.
      * Because of that, forloop.index0 is NOT the letter number. The stagger
        counts real letters itself, with letter_index.

    A space is emitted as a non-breaking space. The parent is a flex container,
    so an ordinary space would collapse and the two words would run together.

    The letters are hidden from assistive tech and the link carries the whole
    name as its label, so a screen reader says "Eric Man" instead of spelling
    it out one span at a time.

    The spans carry NO inline animation-delay any more. Slice 3h set one here
    from a running letter counter; since 3l the stagger is a --i custom
    property written by js/origami.js and turned into a delay in the
    stylesheet. Markup that is inert without JS is the point: with no script
    these are plain spans and the name simply sits there, which is exactly the
    fallback we want. The counter went with the delay — the empty-entry guard
    below is what skips the split's phantom entries, and always was.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign wordmark = site.title | split: "" -%}
  <a class="site-title" href="/" aria-label="{{ site.title }}">
    {%- for ch in wordmark -%}
    {%- if ch != "" -%}
    <span aria-hidden="true">{% if ch == " " %}&#160;{% else %}{{ ch }}{% endif %}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </a>
  <nav class="site-nav">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/">Blog</a></li>
      <li><a href="/archive/">Archive</a></li>
      {%- comment -%}
        "Tags" is back, per Eric in slice 3g — this reverses Q11, which had
        removed it in 3b to keep the settled Q8 set. It sits after Archive and
        before the outbound link, so the internal pages stay grouped.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <li><a href="/tags/">Tags</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://ericman.com">ericman.com</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
</header>
